task.speedup_news_search (completed) {
  the following command is very slow, why:
  /news search rust programming

  do we actually preload all the news articles, if so, stop doing that, we can lazy load it when we click open the article modal

  Why it was slow:
  news_fetch.php ran enrichStoryContent() and enrichStoryImages() over the
  whole selected batch before yielding the first story. For Google News every
  item is a wrapper link with no body, so the list request downloaded and
  parsed every publisher article (with feed/reader/WordPress/proxy/syndication/
  Wayback fallbacks) and every article page again for a lead image.

  Implemented:
  - news_fetch.php: added a `--lazy` list mode. It reuses article bodies and
    images that are already on disk but never touches the network; a story
    whose feed body is only a headline/preview gets its preview cleared so the
    detail view knows it still needs the full text. `--article` is unchanged
    and remains the on-demand path used by the modal.
  - app/chat_server.py: `_stream_news_events` now passes `--lazy` for every
    /news, /news search, /googlenews, and /medium list request.
  - app/chat.html: the story modal already fetched /api/news_article when a
    story arrived without paragraphs; the Learn action now stays disabled
    while that on-demand fetch is in flight so a preview cannot be learned as
    if it were the complete article.

  Verified:
  - A cold Google News search lists 8 stories with no paragraph events in
    ~0.9s (previously 6.1s and 189 preloaded paragraphs for the same batch).
  - Opening one lazy story still resolves its Google News wrapper and returns
    the complete body (40 paragraphs) plus its lead image in ~1.1s on demand.
  - php -l, py_compile, and node --check all pass.
}

task.news_voice_text_to_speech (completed) {
  please reference {directory_of_this_prompt}/../research/text_to_speech.txt:
  - in the news article popup, add a text_to_speech image icon, when click {
    read the content of the news article, paragraph by paragraph
    one paragraph will be sent per time so that we can have a fast response from the text to speech
  }

  Implemented:
  app/chat_server.py
  - Added POST /api/tts. It accepts one article paragraph and returns a cached
    WAV. The local Kokoro pipeline from research/text_to_speech.txt is used
    when installed; otherwise the server falls back to macOS `say`, Linux
    espeak-ng/espeak, and the same cache. The model is warmed in the background
    after startup so the first read-aloud click does not pay the load cost.
  - Audio is cached under .chat/tts_cache by engine, voice, and paragraph text,
    with per-paragraph locks so concurrent prefetches do not synthesize twice.
  app/chat.html
  - Added a speaker icon to the story modal header. Clicking it reads the
    article paragraph by paragraph, prefetching the next paragraph while the
    current one plays, and clicking again stops playback.
  - Very long paragraphs are split at sentence/comma boundaries for fast first
    audio. Read-aloud stops when the story modal closes or another story opens.

  Verified: POST /api/tts returns audio/wav (Kokoro engine, cached on the
  second request); the empty-text request returns HTTP 400; Python compile and
  the browser script syntax check pass.
}

