  }

  please fix it in a systematic way

  Implemented:
  news_fetch.php
  - Article recovery now runs a layered fallback chain instead of stopping at
  the first blocked publisher page: publisher RSS (image + preview),
  Medium reader mirror, WordPress REST API, generic reader proxies (Google
  Translate and Jina Reader), syndicated-copy matching, then Wayback.
  - Added a generic syndication fallback: when a blocked story has a headline,
  search Google News for the same report, match the headline, and use a
  directly accessible partner copy. A short time budget and per-candidate
  timeout keep a burst of blocked stories fast; reader proxies are a second
  pass only when the direct copies are incomplete.
  - Added WordPress REST recovery (`/wp-json/wp/v2/posts?slug=...`), which
  restores NewsNation and other WordPress sites even when the page itself is
  challenged.
  - Added Google Translate and Jina Reader recovery, which restore AP and other
  bot-challenged pages from a different network.
  - Article extraction now rejects bot-challenge/paywall/footer pages, trims
  navigation, ad rails, related-story lists, and legal footers, and keeps the
  longest preview as a last resort instead of showing an empty modal. This also
  restores lead images from feeds/proxies, so the image errors disappear.
  - Added `--title <headline>` to `--article` so an on-demand detail request can
  use the syndication matcher. Bumped `ARTICLE_EXTRACTOR_VERSION` to 8 so old
  failure-cache entries are refetched.
  app/chat_server.py
  - `/api/news_article` accepts `title` and passes it to `news_fetch.php`.
  app/chat.html
  - The detail-modal retry sends the story headline with the article URL.

  Verified with the six reported URLs (cold cache, no stderr diagnostics):
  - Reuters: 12 paragraphs / 2,714 chars + lead image.
  - FT: 15 paragraphs / 4,339 chars + lead image.
  - NYT (Wachtell article): 9 paragraphs / 3,683 chars + lead image.
  - NYT (Trump China trip article): 23 paragraphs / 6,601 chars + lead image.
  - NewsNation: 12 paragraphs / 2,317 chars + lead image.
  - AP: 32 paragraphs / 7,097 chars + lead image.
  `php -l news_fetch.php`, the Python compile check, and the browser script
  syntax check all pass.
}

task.news_chat_do_not_scroll_to_bottom (completed) {
  please learn from task.news_article_scrolled_to_bottom:
  - in the news chat on the right column, after typing a question, the answer should show without scrolling to the answer's bottom

  Implemented:
  app/chat.html
  - The in-modal news chat no longer follows the newest token while an answer
    streams. On send, the new assistant message is pinned so its first line is
    at the top of the message list, and every streaming render re-applies that
    anchor instead of scrolling to the answer's bottom.
  - A reader scroll during streaming releases the pin, so the answer does not
    keep pulling the view back to the top while they read another part of the
    conversation. Programmatic pin scrolls are distinguished from reader
    scrolls, and the pin resets when the chat closes or a story is reopened.
}

task.news_article_scrolled_to_bottom (completed) {
  when we load the news article in the modal, it scrolls to the end of the article, we should let it focus on the top part of the article and do not do the scrolling

  Root cause:
  renderNewsModal() ran before newsPanelEl.hidden was cleared. A scrollTop
  assignment on a display:none subtree is ignored, and the browser restores
  the news body's previous offset when the panel is shown, so opening a story
  after the previous one had been scrolled left the new story at that offset
  (often the end).

  Implemented:
  app/chat.html
  - Added resetNewsBodyScroll(item), which clears the news body scroll offset
    after the panel is visible and again on the next animation frame, guarded
    so a newer story is never reset by an older request.
  - openNewsModal() now shows the panel first and then resets the scroll, so
    every story opens at its top instead of inheriting the previous article's
    position. renderNewsModal() still pins the top while paragraphs stream in.
}

task.bug.news_list_loading_2 (completed) {
  please make sure the following news articles load {
    http://web.archive.org/web/20260211100204id_/https://www.hollywoodintoto.com/clifford-the-big-red-dog-review-2021/
  }
  please make sure to fix it in the systematic way

  Root cause:
  A story whose link is already a Wayback Machine URL was only fetched as the
  archive page. When that request failed (for example archive.org returned 404
  for a snapshot URL carrying an extra query, or rate-limited a burst), the
  existing archive fallback asked the availability API about the archive URL
  itself instead of the publisher URL embedded in its path, so nothing could
  recover and the detail modal stayed empty.

  Implemented:
  news_fetch.php
  - Added parseWaybackUrl(), which recognizes
  /web/<timestamp>[modifier]/<original-url> links, normalizes them to the raw
  "id_" snapshot form, and recovers the embedded publisher URL (including a
  query string that parse_url() attaches to the archive URL).
  - fetchArticleArchiveFallback() now retries the normalized snapshot directly.
  If that still fails, it looks up a snapshot for the embedded original URL
  instead of querying the availability API about the archive URL itself.
  - The snapshot normalizer now also handles modifiers other than "id_" and
  keeps working when the publisher URL already appears in raw form.
  - An empty cached body for a Wayback story is no longer served for the
  failure-cache TTL; the list fetch retries it, so an earlier failed attempt
  cannot keep the story blank.

  Verified:
  - The reported URL loads 20 paragraphs / 1 image through /news and
  `news_fetch.php --json --article`.
  - The same article still loads from the live publisher URL and from a
  non-raw /web/<timestamp>/ form.
  - Simulated a stale empty cache for an archive URL: the list path retried,
  the direct archive request failed with HTTP 404, and the embedded-original
  snapshot fallback recovered all 20 paragraphs.
  - php -l passes.
}

